    <!-- ===== REGISTRATION FAQS ===== -->
    <section id="faq">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="kicker">Registration FAQs</div>
        <h2 class="title">Questions teams ask most often</h2>
        <div class="faqgrid">
          <div>
            <details open>
              <summary>What is the difference between a regional site and an onsite centre?</summary>
              <p>Kanpur, Amritapuri, Chennai, and Mathura are four independent regional sites. Kanpur Multi-Site alone conducts its 2026 onsite contest at three centres: Kanpur, Gandhinagar, and Pune. A centre is a venue within Kanpur Regional Multi-Site, not a separate regional site.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Is there one preliminary contest for the four regional sites?</summary>
              <p>Yes. The ICPC India Preliminary Round is common to Kanpur, Amritapuri, Chennai, and Mathura. Each regional site independently selects from the teams registered for that site.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Should we register and pay separately for each regional site?</summary>
              <p>Yes. Register and pay the applicable registration fee separately for every regional site your team wishes to participate in. A team can participate in a maximum of two regional sites.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Who can form an ICPC team?</summary>
              <p>A team consists of three eligible student contestants and one coach. All contestants and the coach must belong to the same College/institution. Students may be from any eligible academic branch.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can one coach register multiple teams?</summary>
              <p>Yes. A coach may guide and register multiple teams, but every team must have its own three eligible contestants and complete the registration formalities.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
          <div>
            <details>
              <summary>When is a team accepted on the ICPC portal?</summary>
              <p>Acceptance follows verification of the required registration details and payment. The accepted status on the ICPC portal serves as confirmation that the submitted registration has been processed.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>How do we know whether payment was received?</summary>
              <p>Check the team status on the ICPC registration portal and official Kanpur Regional communication. Keep the payment reference and proof available for verification.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Is the registration fee paid by every student?</summary>
              <p>No. The preliminary contest fee is <strong>₹ 1,500/- per team</strong>, not per student. Teams qualifying for the Kanpur Regional onsite round pay an additional <strong>Rs 4,500 per team</strong>. Do not make duplicate payments for the same team and stage.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>How a coach can cancel a team?</summary>
              <p>The coach signs in to the ICPC registration portal, opens the relevant team registration, and uses the cancellation option. Cancellation must follow the official registration schedule.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Do we need to register for Onsite Round again in case we qualify the Preliminay roud</summary>
              <p>Selected teams are promoted from the preliminary round to the regional onsite round. They do not need to create a new team registration, but they must complete the Kanpur Regional onsite fee payments, and document requirements communicated to selected teams.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can we choose our Kanpur Regional onsite centre?</summary>
              <p>Kanpur Regional conducts the onsite contest in Kanpur, Gandhinagar, and Pune. Selected teams receive their centre information through the official selection (YTD) and confirmation communication.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
